<Base title="About — Muhammad Irfan Waseem"><header class="page-head wrap"><p class="eyebrow">BEHIND THE WORK</p><h1>Curiosity meets<br/><em>practical engineering.</em></h1></header><section class="wrap page-body two-column"><img class="portrait" src={url('images/Irfan.webp')} alt="Muhammad Irfan Waseem" width="640" height="800"/><div class="prose"><h2>I’m Muhammad Irfan Waseem.</h2><p>I develop mobile applications with Flutter, Dart and Firebase, with a focus on ordering, inventory and everyday business workflows.</p><p>I study Computer Science at COMSATS University Islamabad, Sahiwal Campus, with graduation expected in 2027. My freelance Flutter work began in January 2025.</p><h2>From an interface to a system</h2><p>Food Fight connects customers, branch teams and delivery riders. My ERP repositories explore the records behind procurement, stock movements, sales and ledgers. TeamSync extends that work into web-based collaboration.</p><p>I care about making these workflows understandable: clear interfaces, structured data and permissions that reflect how people use the software.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href={url('projects/')}>Explore my work</a><a class="button quiet" href={url('experience/')}>Experience & education</a></div></div></section></Base>
